    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "## Fixed \u2705\n\nThe issue was a floating-point precision bug in `src/money.js`. When converting prices to cents (multiplying by 100), JavaScript's floating-point arithmetic was producing `3995.0000000000005` instead of exactly `3995` for a price like 39.95.\n\n**The fix:** I added `Math.round()` to both `parseEuros()` and `cellCents()` functions to ensure the result is always a whole number of cents:\n\n- **Line 13:** `parseEuros()` now does `Math.round(Number(Number(s.replace(/,/g, '')).toFixed(2)) * 100)`\n- **Line 25:** `cellCents()` now does `Math.round(Number(s) * 100)`\n\nAll tests pass, and you can now add subscriptions with prices like 39.95, 12.99, 10.99, etc. without issues.",
